<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ferghana Valley</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fergana-valley">Ferghana</a> Valley is a fertile basin in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/central-asia">Central Asia</a>, today shared by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/uzbekistan">Uzbekistan</a>, Kyrgyzstan and Tajikistan. In the late second century BCE the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/han-dynasty">Han Dynasty</a> sent armies there to obtain its famous 'heavenly horses', extending Chinese influence into Central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/asia">Asia</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ferghana-valley.jpg" alt="Ferghana Valley" width="320" height="161" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: ValleDeFerganáTopográfico.svg by User:Rowanwindwhistler Translated into English by User:CitrusHemlock · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:ValleDeFergan%C3%A1Topogr%C3%A1fico_en.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
